    "generated": "2026-09-11",
    "what_it_is": "Geranyl caproate is a naturally occurring ester, a family of molecules famous for their bright, fruity, and floral aromas. It contributes to the complex scent profiles of certain aromatic herbs and flowers. You are most likely to encounter it as a subtle flavor note in black tea, honey, or the fragrant oils of geraniums and lemongrass.",
    "found_in": "It is naturally present in the essential oils of several fragrant plants, including palmarosa, Syrian oregano, and various species of geranium and thyme.",
    "why_researchers_care": "Researchers are primarily drawn to geranyl caproate for its role as a volatile aroma compound and its interactions with biological systems. Early laboratory work (Oxford level 5, in vitro) is exploring its potential to inhibit specific enzymes and its utility in bioengineering, such as using yeast platforms to synthesize complex molecules like cannabinoids. Entomologists are also investigating how odorants like this one might influence the host-seeking behavior of mosquitoes.",
